HEARD l01 Colorado, 1945, Farmer Lloyd Olson picks a rooster for dinner.
HEARD l02 his mother -in -law is coming, and she loves the neck.
HEARD l03 So Lloyd aims the axe high to leave her as much neck as possible.
HEARD l04 Wack.
HEARD l05 and the chicken just walks away.
HEARD l06 The next morning, Mike is still walking around, trying to pick, trying to crow, with no head.
HEARD l07 Wait, how is that even possible?
HEARD l08 You see, the ax missed the big vein in his neck, and a blood clot stopped the bleeding.
HEARD l09 And it left most of his brainstem, the part that runs breathing, the heartbeat and walking.
HEARD l10 It's like unplugging a computer screen. The screen goes dark, but the computer keeps running.
HEARD l11 So Lloyd feeds him milk and water with an eyedropper, straight down the neck.
HEARD l12 The rooster keeps on growing from 2 .5 pounds to almost 8.
HEARD l13 He goes on tour. People pay 25 cents to see him. Life magazine takes his picture.
HEARD l14 Lloyd makes $4 ,500 a month.
